@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="page-header">
    <div>
        <div class="page-kicker">Privacy and data care</div>
        <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="page-subtitle">
            KiddoCare handles child, parent and kindergarten information with clear role-based access and careful file storage.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="section-panel privacy-panel">
    <h2>Information Stored</h2>
    <p>
        The application stores child profiles, parent and teacher contact details, attendance records,
        daily reports, medical notes, absence notices, consent requests, announcements, events and uploaded child documents.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="section-panel privacy-panel">
    <h2>Access Control</h2>
    <p>
        Access is role-based. Administrators manage kindergarten data, teachers work with their assigned group,
        and parents can view information connected to their own children.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="section-panel privacy-panel">
    <h2>Uploaded Files</h2>
    <p>
        Uploaded photos and documents are stored outside the public Git repository. Local development files are kept under
        protected application storage and should be moved to a dedicated cloud storage provider before production deployment.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="section-panel privacy-panel">
    <h2>Demo Data</h2>
    <p>
        Development demo data is fictional and exists only to test the application workflow. Real child photos,
        personal documents and production passwords should never be committed to source control.
    </p>
</section>
